:: Stumble out the door {"position":"300,175","size":"100,100"}
The way to the cafeteria  is a game of dodging racing speedsters and swerving around mechs buried in their datapads. The Ark isn't too terribly crowded with mechs, the crew being scarce compared to the ships back on Cybertron, but it's most popular corridors aren't spacious enough for all the pede traffic.

The cafeteria is similarly crowded, mechs shuffling to the energon dispenser and filling up tables. Some groups are chatting animatedly, some groups are sitting and reading through reports quietly.

You don't spend enough time looking around before beelining for the dispenser. You're not too hungry, your entire frame still aching for more sleep, but you can't afford to pass out midway through your shift. Again.

The line moves quickly enough before you're able to scan your portable HUD, a loud embarrassing beep and the machine greeting you by designation You duck your helm at the mechanical voice. The dispenser displays your ID code and the number of rations you're allowed for the day: three remaining.

Your share of rations for the entire month are probably much fuller than everyone else's. It's not that you *try* to avoid meal times; you're just really bad at ending your shift. The superior officers have gotten onto you about it more than once.

Your cube filled with the standard-grade energon, you quickly make your way out of the cafeteria to start your shift. If your superiors get onto you about taking rations from the eatery, you'll just say you're holding it for a friend.

[[Start monitor duty]]


:: The Autobots {"position":"675,25","size":"100,100"}
This can show the approval system for the characters.

Prowl: $prowl.approval
 <<if $prowl.approval >=95>>
 		Prowl trusts you with the Autobot cause.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=85 && $prowl.approval <=94>>
		Prowl needs to be near you.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=75 && $prowl.approval <=84>>
		Prowl wants to be around you.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=65 && $prowl.approval <=74>>
		 Prowl sees you as a confidante.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=50 && $prowl.approval <=64>>
		Prowl thinks you are of a similar mind.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=35 && $prowl.approval <=49>>
		Prowl thinks you are better than most.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=25 && $prowl.approval <=34>>
		Prowl thinks you are a fine, reasonable soldier.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=15 && $prowl.approval <=24>>
		Prowl sees you as part of the rabble.
 <<elseif $prowl.approval >=0 && $prowl.approval <=14>>
		Prowl can't tell you apart from the cannon fodder.
 <</if>>

Optimus: $optimus.approval

:)


